---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const CONTACT = "oneabovealldotorg@gmail.com";
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy — oneaboveall"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description="What oneaboveall.org collects, why, who processes it, how long we keep it, and your rights under the GDPR."
  lastUpdated="October 2, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data oneaboveall.org (the "site")
    collects, why, and what rights you have. We try to collect as little as
    possible. We do not sell your data.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller is <strong>Devvally</strong>, based in Spain. For any
    privacy question or request, email
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <h3>If you only visit</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>An aggregate page-view counter.</strong> Each page load adds one
      to a single total. It is not linked to you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Referral parameters.</strong> If you arrive through a link with
      <code>ref</code> or <code>utm_*</code> parameters (for example from a
      creator), we store them in your browser's local storage, and count the
      visit against that referral code (a number, not a profile of you).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your theme choice</strong> (light/dark), in local storage.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical logs</strong> our servers keep for security and
      troubleshooting (such as IP address and request time).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>If you sign in and bid</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your name and email address</strong> from Google or Apple
      sign-in (we never see your Google or Apple password).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your display name</strong>, which is shown publicly while you
      lead a round, while you hold the seat, and on the leaderboard and
      history.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your bids and their payment status</strong> (amount, time,
      authorized / charged / released). Card details are entered directly into
      Stripe; we never receive your full card number.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>First-touch referral data</strong> (the <code>ref</code> /
      <code>utm_*</code> values you first arrived with), attached to your
      account so we know which creators bring bidders.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A session cookie</strong> that keeps you signed in. It is
      strictly necessary for the service, so we don't ask for consent for
      it. We use no advertising or third-party tracking cookies.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>If you win</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your photo</strong> and any description of how you'd like your
      character drawn. Your raw photo is private: only you and we can access
      it. Only the redrawn artwork is shown publicly.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>An optional social link</strong>, shown publicly on the
      champion card.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Why we use it, and our legal basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>To run the auction and deliver what you paid for</strong>
      (account, bids, holds and charges, showing your name, redrawing the
      artwork with your photo, emails telling you you've been outbid or won)
      — <em>performance of our contract with you</em> (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To keep payment and accounting records</strong> —
      <em>legal obligation</em> (Art. 6(1)(c)), e.g. Spanish tax law.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To measure which referral links and creators work, prevent
      fraud and abuse, moderate content and keep the site secure</strong> —
      our <em>legitimate interests</em> (Art. 6(1)(f)). You can object at any
      time (see your rights below).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your photo</strong> is used only to make the artwork, because you
      upload it for that purpose and confirm you have the right to do so.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Who processes your data for us</h2>
  <p>We share data only with service providers that help us run the site, under data-processing terms:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — card payments, authorization holds and fraud prevention.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> and <strong>Apple</strong> — sign-in, if you choose them.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> — sending our emails (outbid / won notifications).</li>
    <li><strong>Hetzner</strong> — hosting our servers and database in the EU.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose data where the law requires it, or to protect our
    rights (for example, in a payment dispute).
  </p>

  <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our servers are in the EU. Some providers above (such as Stripe, Google,
    Apple and Resend) may process data in the United States or elsewhere.
    Where they do, the transfer is covered by the EU–US Data Privacy
    Framework or the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account data</strong> (name, email, display name, referral
      data): while your account is active, and deleted when you ask us to
      delete it — except what we must keep below.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Bids and payment records</strong>: as long as tax and
      accounting law requires (in Spain, generally up to 6 years).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your photo</strong>: while you are or have been the champion,
      so the archive of past scenes stays accurate, and deleted on request.
      Artwork that was already published may remain in the archive, but we
      will remove your name and link from it on request.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Server logs</strong>: a short period, typically no more than 30 days.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local storage</strong> (theme, referral) stays in your browser
      until you clear it; the session cookie expires when you sign out or
      after it lapses.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>give you a copy of your data (access) and send it to you in a portable format;</li>
    <li>correct inaccurate data;</li>
    <li>delete your data;</li>
    <li>restrict how we use it, or object to processing based on our legitimate interests.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> and we'll reply within
    one month. If you're unhappy with how we handle your data, you can
    complain to the Spanish data protection authority, the
    <strong>Agencia Española de Protección de Datos (AEPD)</strong>,
    <a href="https://www.aepd.es" rel="noopener">www.aepd.es</a>, or to the
    authority in the country where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>8. We don't sell your data</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell or rent personal data, and we don't use it for third-party
    advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is not for children. You must be 18 or older to sign in and bid,
    and photos of anyone under 18 are not allowed. If you believe a minor has
    given us data, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version;
    if a change is significant we'll point it out on the site or by email.
  </p>

  <p>See also our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
